  "output": {
    "answer": "Nothing does, and I said so myself in the write-up. Truth there is only my own taps — one tapper, five days of streams, mostly English cards, so Japanese is barely tested. I also flagged selection bias: I may tap more when a pick is clearly wrong or clearly right than when it's ambiguous, which skews the sample toward easy calls. And with only 87 lots (69 non-locked), every interval is wide, roughly plus or minus ten to twelve points. So the 65.2% is real but unverified by anyone outside me, and I know that's the next thing to fix, not something I've resolved.",
